  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## The precise untwisting relation for [3,1,0]²\n\nSame notation as the adjoint notebook: rows $(\\alpha,i,j)$ with $(i,j)\\in\\{(1,3),(1,2),(2,3)\\}$, and Q-functions regularized to the monic untwisted staggered ones. There are two changes from the adjoint:\n- **Measure.** Every bracket is a contour around the full ladder $\\theta_s+\\{0,1,2,3\\}$.\n- **Column basis.** $H=(c_1+c_3,\\;c_5-c_6+7c_3,\\;c_2-c_3)$ and $O=(c_4,\\;c_6+c_3,\\;c_3)$; the 7 is $2(\\lambda_1-\\lambda_3+1)-1$ of the site rep.\n\n1. **Laplace split.** $\\det N_{\\rm reg}=-\\det[A_1]_O\\,\\det[A_2]_H\\,(1+O(\\varepsilon))$ for all 10 highest-weight states.\n2. **Periodic block.** $\\det[A_2]_H\\to\\det[A_2]^{\\rm untw}_H$, at rate exactly $O(\\varepsilon)$.\n3. **Bare block.**\n$$\\det[A_1]_O=V_\\lambda(z)\\,E_\\lambda\\,(1+O(\\varepsilon)),\\qquad E_\\lambda=-\\frac{(\\lambda_1-\\lambda_2+1)(\\lambda_2-\\lambda_3+1)}{(\\lambda_1-\\lambda_3+1)!\\,(\\lambda_1-\\lambda_2)!\\,(\\lambda_2-\\lambda_3)!}.$$\n   This is **the same function of the total weight as for the adjoint**. The bare-row powers are $\\max(0,\\,6-d_{ij})$, where $6=2(\\lambda_1-\\lambda_3)_{\\rm site}$ replaces the adjoint's 4.\n\n**Result** (identical in form to the adjoint):\n$$\\boxed{\\lim_{\\varepsilon\\to0}\\frac{V_{\\lambda_{\\rm vac}}(z)}{V_{\\lambda_A}(z)}\\frac{\\langle L_A|R_A\\rangle}{\\langle L_A|0\\rangle\\langle0|R_A\\rangle}=\\frac{\\mathcal B_{\\lambda_A}}{\\mathcal B_{\\lambda_{\\rm vac}}},\\qquad \\mathcal B_\\lambda=\\frac{E_\\lambda\\det\\mathcal N}{c^{\\rm ref}\\Psi^{\\rm ref}}}$$\n$\\mathcal N$ is the $3\\times3$ matrix of untwisted periodic brackets with columns $\\langle q^{j}(u+1)q_i-q^jq_i\\rangle$, $\\langle u\\,q^jq_i(u-1)-(u-7)\\,q^j(u+1)q_i\\rangle$ and $\\langle q^jq_i(u-1)-q^j(u+1)q_i\\rangle$.\n\n**Evidence.**\n- **P1** $\\theta=(1/3,-8/57)$: $E$ agrees with its numerical value to $\\sim10^{-18}$ for all 10 states (the doublets included). The boxed ratio matches the physical limit to $\\sim10^{-19}$. Split residual $O(\\varepsilon)$; three $\\varphi$.\n- **P2** $\\theta=(1/5,46/55)$, $\\varphi=(3/2,1/2,-2)$: split and periodic block $\\sim10^{-7}$ at $\\varepsilon=10^{-8}$; $E_\\lambda$ formula to $10^{-12.4}$–$10^{-13.4}$ (two-point extrapolation); exact identity to working precision.\n\n$E_\\lambda$ was carried over from the adjoint notebook, not refitted. Here it is **independently validated** on 8 new weights at two chain points, but it is still not derived.\n\n## Matching to bare untwisted eigenvectors\n\nFor rational $t$, $\\theta=(t,0)$ puts the poles at $t+n$ and $n$, so every bracket is exactly $a+b\\,e^{2\\pi it}$. The formula is therefore evaluated **exactly**, with $\\omega=e^{2\\pi it}$ kept symbolic, and the ratio $\\mathcal B_A/\\mathcal B_{\\rm vac}$ is checked to be $\\omega$-independent. For the two doublets the values lie in $\\mathbb Q(\\sqrt D)$, so their symmetric functions are fitted instead.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 12. Explicit Q-formula (exact) and exact untwisted eigenvectors at theta = (t, 0). ---- *)\nClearAll[SdiagF, S2F, buildAtF, bracketExactF, BexactF, BratioF, siteWtF, compIdxF, tValsF, dataAtF];\n\n(* E_ji = S^-1 E_ij^T S with S diagonal, S_11 = 1. *)\nSdiagF = Module[{s, sv = Array[s, dsF]},\n   sv /. First@Solve[Join[{s[1] == 1}, Flatten@Table[Thread[Flatten[DiagonalMatrix[sv].Normal[EEF[j, i]] - Transpose[Normal[EEF[i, j]]].DiagonalMatrix[sv]] == 0],\n        {ij, {{1, 2}, {2, 3}}}, {i, {ij[[1]]}}, {j, {ij[[2]]}}]], sv]];\nS2F = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[SdiagF, SdiagF]];\n\n(* Rebuild the chain, measure and untwisted states at theta = {t, 0}. *)\nbuildAtF[t_] := (buildChainF[{t, 0}]; setMeasureF[\"ladder\"]; untwF = buildUntwF[];);\n\n(* Exact bracket: site-1 poles t+n carry om = e^{2 pi i t}, site-2 poles n carry 1. *)\nbracketExactF[f_] := With[{poles = Flatten@Table[th + n, {th, thetaF}, {n, lamSiteF[[3]], lamSiteF[[1]]}]},\n   Sum[If[MemberQ[thetaF[[1]] + Range[lamSiteF[[3]], lamSiteF[[1]]], p], om, 1] f[p]/Times @@ (p - DeleteCases[poles, p]), {p, poles}]];\n(* B_lambda = E_lambda det(calN)/(c^ref Psi^ref), the boxed formula; c7 = 2(l1-l3+1)-1. *)\nBexactF[s_] := Module[{q, qd, lam = s[\"mu\"], Nm, psi, cref, c7 = 2 (lamSiteF[[1]] - lamSiteF[[3]] + 1) - 1},\n   q = Function[{i, x}, qpolyF[s[\"q\"][[i]], x]];\n   qd = Function[{j, x}, qpolyF[s[\"qd\"][[j]], x]];\n   Nm = Table[{\n      bracketExactF[Function[x, qd[ij[[2]], x + 1] q[ij[[1]], x] - qd[ij[[2]], x] q[ij[[1]], x]]],\n      bracketExactF[Function[x, x qd[ij[[2]], x] q[ij[[1]], x - 1] - (x - c7) qd[ij[[2]], x + 1] q[ij[[1]], x]]],\n      bracketExactF[Function[x, qd[ij[[2]], x] q[ij[[1]], x - 1] - qd[ij[[2]], x + 1] q[ij[[1]], x]]]}, {ij, tripleF}];\n   psi = Product[psiRefLocF[Function[i, Function[x, q[i, x]]], th, 1, 2], {th, thetaF}];\n   cref = Product[cRefLocF[Function[j, Function[x, qd[j, x]]], th, 3, 2], {th, thetaF}];\n   EformulaF[lam] Det[Nm]/(cref psi)];\n(* B_A/B_vac at om = -1, together with its difference from om = 2 (must be 0). *)\nBratioF[m_] := With[{r = Function[w, RootReduce[(BexactF[untwF[[m]]] /. om -> w)/(BexactF[untwF[[1]]] /. om -> w)]]},\n   {r[-1], RootReduce[r[-1] - r[2]]}];\n\n(* Canonical component of r_0: site-1 hw (x) the unique site-2 vector of weight lambda_A - (3,1,0), if that weight space is 1-dim. *)\nsiteWtF = Transpose[Table[Diagonal[Normal@EEF[i, i]], {i, 3}]];\ncompIdxF[lam_] := With[{pos = Flatten@Position[siteWtF, lam - repF]}, If[Length[pos] == 1, pos[[1]], None]];\n\ntValsF = {9/19, -9/19, 3/11, -3/11, 5/31, 21/59, 8/19, 2/7};\ndataAtF = Table[(buildAtF[t];\n    {t, Table[BratioF[m], {m, 10}], Table[With[{r0 = untwF[[m, \"vec\"]], c = compIdxF[untwF[[m, \"mu\"]]]},\n       If[c === None, None, RootReduce[r0.(S2F r0)/r0[[c]]^2]]], {m, 10}]}), {t, tValsF}];\n\nColumn[{\n  Grid[{{\"S (E_ji = S^-1 E_ij^T S)\", Row[SdiagF, \",\"]},\n    {\"B_A/B_vac independent of om = e^{2 pi i t} (all t, all 10 states)\", And @@ Flatten[Table[d[[2, m, 2]] === 0, {d, dataAtF}, {m, 10}]]},\n    {\"even in t (t = +-9/19, +-3/11)\", And @@ Flatten[Table[RootReduce[Total[dataAtF[[p, 2, All, 1]]] - Total[dataAtF[[p + 1, 2, All, 1]]]] === 0, {p, {1, 3}}]]},\n    {\"t = 9/19 (P1) vs physical limit psi0NormF, max rel.\", N[Max[Abs[N[dataAtF[[1, 2, All, 1]], 60]/psi0NormF - 1]], 3]}},\n   Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n  Grid[Prepend[Table[{d[[1]], Sequence @@ (N[d[[2, All, 1]], 8])}, {d, dataAtF}], Prepend[nameF, \"t\"]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
